    "sections": {
        "description": "A block theme for software companies and startups, built on the Core Forms design system. Hassium is element 108, first made in a lab in Darmstadt a few atoms at a time, and the theme is for small teams who build that way. It pairs Inter with Hedvig Letters Serif headings, puts one brand color on everything that asks to be clicked, and ships a frosted sticky header, dark and brand bands, screenshot frames, pricing tables, changelogs, and complete landing pages. Includes 67 patterns, six designs, three heading presets, core blocks only, and no JavaScript of its own."
    },
